{
  "id": "e05",
  "rule": "media upload refusals before anything is stored: the create permission chain in WordPress's order (id, author, sticky, upload_files, the parent, the declared image type), the parent's type (an attachment; a revision has no post id in QuarkPress, D31), multipart bodies without a usable file part (another name, file[] and file[a], an empty file name), Content-MD5 forms, the raw body's header checks and file name, JSON bodies (url included, D39) and unreadable multipart bodies; the collection's Allow following the create check (r21); refusals only, nothing is stored on either side (the accepted raw uploads are compared from the stored-upload task on)",
